+# GameFinder development instructions
+
+Maintain the approved product, not a competing redesign. Preserve Find, Vault, Discover, Profile, existing navigation and Finn identity. Player count, youngest age suitability and maximum playtime are hard constraints; standard vibes rank eligible games with closest-match fallback. Preserve seven equally weighted descriptive dimensions on the 1–5 half-point scale and six distinct vibe constructs. Return up to three owned and three unowned games; rerolls exclude prior results; Surprise Me uses owned games independently of filters. Keep scan review/confirmation and manual fallback; do not retain or repurpose recognition photos. Free Vault capacity is 50. Premium is $4.99 monthly or $44.99 annually; no lifetime plan. Protect paid features server-side, including Finn teaching and questions, and preserve five approved lesson chapters. Keep original assets, provenance and rating review distinctions intact. Do not invent verified rules or evidence. Never include credentials, private business documents or personal data in commits. Work on authorized development branches; no force pushes, merging main, publishing releases, spending, or changing locked product requirements without owner approval. Run targeted regression tests and typecheck; report skipped tests and blockers accurately. Treat current implementation as evidence, not authority to change requirements.
